'' RUN: a header an '#import' already read (sys/win's windows.bi), then '#include'd by the
'' program itself, is the program's own: the skipped include hands it, and every header it
'' read, back (src/pp/ppindex.tiko PpImportReadOwn_). Its CONTEXT beats 'using tasks' with no
'' TKO0919, as in tasks-win-own-wins. Without this, sys/win/direct2d's 'AS GUID' was TKO0919
'' against sys/win/com's Guid function, and the toolchain's sys/win verify failed.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 -mt -i toolchains/tiko-windows/inc tests/modules/src/taskswin/own-after-import.tiko -o tests/modules/taskswinownafterimport.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-NOT: TKO0919
'' EXPECT-FILE: tests/modules/taskswinownafterimport.exe
'' RUN: tests/modules/taskswinownafterimport.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: -1false
